      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>The Most Spoken Language</h3>Have you ever noticed that the same patterns repeat everywhere - in the spirals of a sunflower, in the rhythm of your heartbeat, in the distance between planets? We can consider mathematics as the language of nature; it is present in all places, whether we notice it or not.</p><p>As we study mathematics, we come to understand how nature works. With this knowledge, we can create, among other things, the electronic device you are using to learn right now.</p><p>In this lesson, we will explore where numbers appear in our world - from our own bodies to the farthest stars. Along the way, we will see that humanity has been learning the language of nature through mistakes and successes that helped us understand the universe.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_inus",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>In Us</h3>We have already seen that we can use numbers with our hands, but numbers go far beyond our fingers. Try it right now: how many arms do you have? How many eyes? How many teeth can you feel with your tongue? Each of these is a number hiding in your own body. Look at Figure 1 below and see how many parts we can count.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgHumanBody\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgHumanBody', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\" style=\"width: 30%;\" /><b>Figure 1</b>: Human body with its numbered parts.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_intexts",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><h3>In Our Texts</h3>Right now, as you read this sentence, numbers are hidden in it. Try counting: this paragraph has about 40 words. The letter 'e' appears more often than 'z'. Numbers are present in every text we read.</p><p>But not all texts use the alphabet we know. Ancient civilizations created their own writing systems. For example, the Maya used hieroglyphs on stone monuments, like the stela at Copán, Honduras (<htcite0>; <htcite1>). And yes, we can count those hieroglyphs too - numbers appear everywhere, even in ancient stones.</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "1e007481-9bd3-4a09-ad4d-6e812fe79641",
                     "text": "Instituto Hondureño de Antropologia e Historia",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "02",
                        "day": "01"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5390fa3b-735f-4e22-ac98-178303a13fdb",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Writing",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "-1",
                        "day": "-1"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img id=\"imgCopanText\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgCopanText', '0%')\" class=\"imgcenter\" style=\"width: 30%;\" /><b>Figure 2</b>: Stela, altar and hieroglyphs in the form of a staircase at Copán, Honduras (<htcite0>).</p>",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 0,
                     "uuid": "1e007481-9bd3-4a09-ad4d-6e812fe79641",
                     "text": "Instituto Hondureño de Antropologia e Historia",
